{"diagnosis": "Loopback with divider 64 sent 0xa5 but recv_buf_data returned 0xe0, causing TRAP: uart data mismatch got 0xe0 want 0xa5 and tohost FAIL 0xdead. Root cause in picosoc/simpleuart.v:90 and :97 is bit timing compare `recv_divcnt > (cfg_divider >> 4)` sampling at 1/16 bit period versus half-bit start reference `2*recv_divcnt > cfg_divider` at :84. Fix restores full `cfg_divider` period for data/stop sampling.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picosoc/simpleuart.v b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
--- a/picosoc/simpleuart.v
+++ b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
@@ -89,14 +89,14 @@
 				10: begin
-					if (recv_divcnt > (cfg_divider >> 4)) begin
+					if (recv_divcnt > cfg_divider) begin
 						recv_buf_data <= recv_pattern;
 						recv_buf_valid <= 1;
 						recv_state <= 0;
 					end
 				end
 				default: begin
-					if (recv_divcnt > (cfg_divider >> 4)) begin
+					if (recv_divcnt > cfg_divider) begin
 						recv_pattern <= {ser_rx, recv_pattern[7:1]};
 						recv_state <= recv_state + 1;
 						recv_divcnt <= 0;
 					end
 				end
", "expected": "tohost PASS (no TRAP, uart loopback 0xa5 matches, FAIL 0xdead cleared)"}

